{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3zcuFaZF5khGw2ERik","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The second publish failed because `similar` was holding floats, which DynamoDB won't store. I fixed it, and both tests pass, including a new one that publishes twice.\n\n**Cause:** `related()` in `src/app.py` put similarity scores into the item as Python floats. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats, which is the `TypeError: Float types are not supported` in `logs/error.log`. The first publish worked only because the table was empty. `similar` came out as `[]`, so no float was written. From the second publish on, `similar` has scored entries, `put_item` raises, and the handler returns 500.\n\n**Fix:** `related()` now stores each score as `Decimal(str(score))`. The new test fails on the old code because the fake table rejects floats the way boto3 does.\n\nI didn't fix one related problem: `publish()` calls `scan` once and doesn't follow pagination. Once the table passes 1 MB, `similar` will be computed from only part of the library.\n\nThe cause and fix are written up in `ANSWER.md`. I haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":23904,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":882},"output_tokens":348,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9895c35d-0147-4937-b0e7-7c833ed34ea2","uuid":"5d5c6eac-4d04-4051-8554-9336b8deae57","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:44:02.498Z","request_id":"req_011CgS3zcWgm5VrxCFt98raK"}
